Collection of tools to manage movies.

## Setup

Install the development dependencies with uv:

```powershell
uv sync
```

Run the test suite:

```powershell
uv run pytest
```

Create and validate runtime directories and optional platform support:

```powershell
uv run mutils-setup
uv run mutils-setup --check-only
uv run mutils-setup --json
```

## CLI Usage

All tools can still run interactively with no arguments. They also accept
command-line arguments through package console scripts:

```powershell
uv run mdiffer "D:\Movies" "E:\Movies"
uv run mremover "D:\Movies" .nfo --dry-run --exclude "D:\Movies\keep,comma"
uv run mremover "D:\Movies" .nfo --yes --exclude "D:\Movies\keep"
uv run mrenamer "D:\Movies" --dry-run
uv run mrenamer "D:\Movies" --yes
uv run msymlinker "D:\Movies" "Movie (2023)" "E:\Links" "Movie (2023)"
uv run mutils-setup --check-only
uv run mwui
```

The old top-level scripts remain as compatibility wrappers, so commands like
`uv run python mremover.py ...` still work.

mdiffer - displays duplicate movie names between two directories. Results are
written to the repository-local output directory. Existing result and log files
are preserved by creating a new suffixed file when needed.

mremover - recursively removes files with a given extension from a directory,
including matching files directly inside the source directory. Extension
matching is case-insensitive by default. Optional comma-separated exclusions can
skip protected paths in the GUI/TUI. In CLI mode, use repeated `--exclude`
flags so excluded paths may contain commas. Use the preview prompt before
deleting; deleting without a preview requires typing `DELETE` interactively or
passing `--yes` in CLI mode.

mrenamer - renames scene-style movie folders and files to the `Title (Year)`
format. If a rename fails after earlier renames have succeeded, the tool
attempts to roll back the completed renames and reports what was applied and
rolled back. Exact entries named `subs` or `sample` are skipped because scene
releases commonly use those names for non-movie content.

msymlinker - symlinks a folder from a new location to the original location.
On Windows, symlink creation may require Developer Mode or an elevated shell.

mutils-setup - creates and checks the runtime `log/` and `output/` directories,
verifies required imports, reports optional GUI/TUI support, and checks symlink
capability. Optional platform checks are reported as warnings rather than hard
failures.

mwui - starts a dependency-free browser UI at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` by
default. The web UI exposes `mdiffer`, `mremover`, `mrenamer`, and `msymlinker`.
Delete and rename actions default to preview mode and require typing `CONFIRM`
before the web UI will run them destructively. The top-level `mwui.py` wrapper
also works with `uv run python mwui.py`.

## Layout

The implementation lives in the `mutils` package. Top-level files such as
`mremover.py` are thin compatibility wrappers around package entry points.
